From: Marionette <marionette@localhost>
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] carry the descriptor TSF into the AWDL sink's radiotap

The sink's radiotap header has only a CHANNEL field:

	present = 0x08, it_len = 12

filin reads TSFT from that header to build its TSF bridge:

	let rx_time_us = radiotap.tsft
	    .map(|hw_tsft| bridge.timestamp_rx(hw_tsft, host_now_us))
	    .unwrap_or(host_now_us);

With no TSFT it always falls back to host time, so `/status` reports

	"tsf_offset_us":0, "synced":false, "aw_alignment_pct":0

Peer discovery still works (peer_count 3-4, neighbor entries installed), but
the availability windows never line up, and file transfer cannot start without
that alignment.

The timestamp is already in the descriptor: `dp_rx_mon_deliver()` has
`mon_pdev->ppdu_info.rx_status.tsft` in scope -- the CBF path a few lines above
reads exactly that field -- so pass it through `marionette_monitor_post_frame()`
into the sink.

Radiotap layout when a timestamp is present:

	offset  0  version 0, pad
	offset  2  it_len = 24
	offset  4  present = 0x09  (TSFT | CHANNEL)
	offset  8  TSFT, 8 bytes LE
	offset 16  channel frequency, channel flags
	offset 20  padding, so the 802.11 header stays 8-byte aligned

When the descriptor carries no timestamp the header keeps its old 12-byte
CHANNEL-only shape, so nothing that worked before changes.

